# Build context for backend/Dockerfile and backend/Dockerfile.dev (context = this directory).
# Both end in `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is baked into the image -- and the
# production image is published. Keep secrets, local state and test-only files out.
#
# Must stay IN the context: src/, alembic/, alembic.ini, requirements*.txt, pyproject.toml and
# docker-entrypoint*.sh (the Dockerfiles and entrypoints use them).

# Secrets / local configuration. The app reads `.env` from its working directory, so a developer's
# backend/.env would otherwise ship inside the image. Configure containers through real
# environment variables (docker-compose.yml `environment:` / the root .env) instead.
.env
.env.*
.env-*
*.pem
*.key

# Virtualenvs and Python build/cache output
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests and their output (the dev stack bind-mounts ./backend, so tests are still there in dev)
tests/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.scannerwork/
*.log

# Local data that must never be published (collection exports, downloaded bulk data).
# .dockerignore patterns are anchored to the context root, so these match backend/data and
# backend/*.csv only -- NOT src/data/, which the app needs.
data/
image-cache/
*.dlens
*.csv

# Not needed inside the image
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.dev
.dockerignore
.git
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
